## Rental Management API

Tracks rental stock items individually with searchable unique IDs, adjustable rent by type, availability control, and transaction history.

Base URL: `/api` (auth required)

### Data Model

- `rental_items`
  - `id`, `unique_code` (unique), `name`
  - `base_rent_amount`, `rent_type` (`day|week|month`), `rent_date` (nullable)
  - `status` (`Available|Rented`)
- `rental_item_transactions`
  - `id`, `rental_item_id`, `action` (`rented|returned`)
  - `rent_date`, `return_date`, `rent_type`, `rent_amount`, `note`

Rent calculation: base is treated as monthly-equivalent; computed amount is:
- day = base / 30
- week = base / 4
- month = base

### Endpoints

#### Create Item

POST `/api/rental-items`
```json
{ "unique_code": "DRL-001", "name": "Drill Machine", "base_rent_amount": 3000, "rent_type": "month" }
```

#### List/Search

GET `/api/rental-items?status=Available&unique_code=DRL`

#### Show Item

GET `/api/rental-items/{id}`

#### Update Item

PUT `/api/rental-items/{id}`

#### Delete Item

DELETE `/api/rental-items/{id}` (not allowed when status is `Rented`)

#### Mark as Rented

POST `/api/rental-items/{id}/rent`
```json
{ "rent_type": "week", "rent_date": "2025-11-03", "note": "Rented to client X" }
```
Behavior: sets status to `Rented`, stores computed `rent_amount` in transactions, hides from Available list.

#### Return Item

POST `/api/rental-items/{id}/return`
```json
{ "return_date": "2025-11-10", "note": "Returned in good condition" }
```
Behavior: sets status back to `Available` and logs transaction.

### Tips

- Search by `unique_code` substring to quickly locate an item.
- The item detail includes recent `transactions` for quick history.


